.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- mango window module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBwindow\fR module displays the title and app ID of the currently focused window in the Mango compositor.\&
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Addressed by \fBmango/window\fR
.PP
\fBformat\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: {title} 
.br
The format string.\& See \fBFORMAT REPLACEMENTS\fR.\&
.PP
\fBrewrite\fR: 
.br
typeof: object 
.br
Rules to rewrite the window title.\& Each key is a regular expression and its value is the replacement string.\& Captures can be used with \fB$1\fR, \fB$2\fR, etc.\&
.PP
\fBicon\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Whether to show the application icon.\&
.PP
\fBicon\-size\fR: 
.br
typeof: integer 
.br
default: 24 
.br
Size of the application icon in pixels.\&
.PP
\fBexpand\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables the module to consume all leftover space.\&
.PP
.SH FORMAT REPLACEMENTS
.PP
\fB{title}\fR: The current window title.\&
.PP
\fB{app_id}\fR: The app ID of the focused window.\&
.PP
.SH REWRITE RULES
.PP
If the title matches a regular expression from the \fBrewrite\fR object, it is replaced by the corresponding value.\& Regular expression syntax follows ECMAScript rules.\& Unmatched titles are left unchanged.\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"mango/window": {
	"format": "{title}",
	"rewrite": {
		"(\&.*) \- Mozilla Firefox": "🌎 $1",
		"(\&.*) \- zsh": "> [$1]"
	},
	"icon": true,
	"icon\-size": 20
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
